● Findings

  - ⚠️ Real bug caught and fixed: tenant reassignment via UpdateUser silently
  no-op'd while reporting success, due to a
  struct-refetch-clobbers-pending-write ordering issue. This would not have been
  caught by any test I'd written earlier (my unit tests only covered
  CreateUser's force-assignment, never UpdateUser's actual persistence) — only
  running the real app end-to-end surfaced it. Now fixed with a regression test.
  - The TanStack Router Devtools overlay (dev-mode only) sits exactly on top of
  every drawer's "Save changes" button, intercepting pointer clicks. Not a
  production bug (devtools don't ship to prod), but it broke naive Playwright
  clicks twice during this session — worth knowing if anyone else automates this
  UI in dev mode.
  - Zero browser console errors across the entire flow except the two I
  deliberately triggered via probes (expected 403 network failures).
  - The DELETE-channel 403 for a foreign tenant's resource is currently enforced
  by a different mechanism (pre-existing ChannelSensitiveWrite permission gate)
  than GET/PUT (my AssertSameTenant check). Both correctly block, but if that
  unrelated permission is ever granted to a tenant-admin in the future, only my
  AssertSameTenant check would remain as the tenant boundary for DELETE — worth
  being aware of, not a bug today.
  - Didn't reach a full click-through of the channel edit drawer's tenant field
  (spent time hunting for the right DOM click target in a card-grid layout with
  no obvious edit affordance); substituted equivalent API-level verification
  through the same authenticated session instead, which exercises the identical
  backend code path.

